// CPT Coding Proficiency — Practice Paper 1
// IMPORTANT PROVENANCE NOTE: CPT (Current Procedural Terminology) is a code
// SET published by the AMA, not a standalone certification — there is no
// official "CPT exam" with a published blueprint the way there is for CCS/
// AWS SAA/Security+. This paper is honestly framed as a topic-mastery
// proficiency test over the CPT codebook's own real, official structure:
// its six Category I sections (Evaluation & Management, Anesthesia,
// Surgery, Radiology, Pathology & Laboratory, Medicine) plus modifiers and
// NCCI coding-edit concepts. Weighting (20/10/30/10/10/10/10 across 100
// questions) reflects Surgery's real size/complexity dominance in the actual
// codebook and typical coder workload emphasis on E/M — it is an authoring
// judgment call, not a replication of any named certification body's exam
// blueprint. Every question tests durable coding LOGIC/RULES/CONVENTIONS
// (global surgical package rules, modifier definitions, NCCI bundling
// logic, E/M leveling concepts) rather than specific numeric code lookups
// that date quickly with each annual CPT code-set update.
// SOURCE: authored from the AMA's published CPT codebook structure/
// conventions and standard, stable coding-guideline knowledge — not copied
// from the CPT codebook's copyrighted code descriptions or any official
// certification exam question bank.

